==Strategy==
At the beginning, stall the Super Metal Hippoe as best as you can with meatshields. When it gets closer to your base, start spawning [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster Cat]]. After a few tries, it will [[Freeze]] the Super Metal Hippoe, at which point you can keep stacking more Hoopmasters until it is perma-stalled. Once Frozen, max out your wallet and start stacking [[Long Distance]] attackers like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], or [[Wave Attack]]ing units like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs Cat]]. When you have a large enough stack of units, start sending out [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] to kill the Super Metal Hippoe. Your stack should be able to clear out every enemy with ease, typically just leaving the Professor A. as the last thing standing. Bring some units such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] or [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter Cat]] to deal with him.

